<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ CPI rose 0.1 pct in June qtr, 1.1 pct in yr.</title>
<headline>NZ CPI rose 0.1 pct in June qtr, 1.1 pct in yr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Tuesday released the following data on the Consumers Price Index to June 1997:</p>
<p>Quarter-on-quarter CPI -</p>
<p>    June 1997		    Mar 1997		 June 1996</p>
<p>    0.1 pct		     -0.3 pct		  +0.8 pct</p>
<p>Year-on-year CPI -</p>
<p>    June 1997		   Mar 1997		  June 1996</p>
<p>    1.1 pct		     +1.8 pct		  +2.0 pct</p>
<p>Year-on-year all groups excluding credit services</p>
<p>    June 1997		   Mar 1997		  June 1996</p>
<p>    +1.5 pct		    +2.0 pct		  +2.3 pct</p>
<p>Qtr-on-qtr excluding housing and credit services -</p>
<p>    June 1997		   Mar 1997		  June 1996</p>
<p>    +0.2 pct		    +0.1 pct		  +0.7 pct</p>
<p>Year-on-year excluding housing and credit services -</p>
<p>    June 1997		   Mar 1997		  June 1996</p>
<p>    +1.2 pct		    +1.7 pct		  +1.4 pct</p>
<p>Note - Economists polled by Reuters predicted on average a 0.14 percent rise in the June quarter CPI, for an annual rise of 1.13 percent. They forecast a 0.33 percent quarterly rise in underlying inflation (which excludes government charges, changes in interest rate charges, and one-offs) for an annual increase of 1.50 percent.</p>
<p>In its June Monetary Policy Statement, the Reserve Bank forecast underlying inflation at 0.3 percent in the June quarter.  </p>
<p>Contributions of commodity groups to CPI quarterly movements:</p>
<p>				    Jun 1997	Mar 1997    Jun 1996</p>
<p>    Food			    0.38	     0.7	   0.9</p>
<p>    Housing			 0.76	     0.3	   1.3</p>
<p>    Household operation	 0.39	     0.2	   0.6</p>
<p>    Apparel			 0.52	    -1.1	   0.8</p>
<p>    Transport		    -1.11	    -0.9	   0.2</p>
<p>    Tobacco/Alcohol	     0.54	     0.7	   0.4</p>
<p>    Personal &amp; health care    0.56	     0.5	   1.0</p>
<p>    Recreation, education     0.81	     0.9	   0.5</p>
<p>    Credit services	    -2.26	    -5.4	   1.0</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom (64 4 4734746) REUTER</p>
</text>
